Compile out Kimchi's self-update: Nix owns the binary, and the store copy is
read-only. Both update gates are hardwired off, `/update` and the auto-update
tip read the same gate so they say updates are managed by Nix, and `--help`
stops listing the now-inert `KIMCHI_NO_UPDATE_CHECK`. The `opts.signal!`
assertion keeps TypeScript's narrowing in the now-unreachable launch path.

